 "title": "Why far away sites feel slow: CDN",
 "sources": [
  "Cloudflare Learning, 'What is a CDN?' (https://www.cloudflare.com/learning/cdn/what-is-a-cdn/, fetched 2026-11-24): 'A content delivery network (CDN) is a geographically distributed group of servers that caches content close to end users'; a CDN 'cuts down on origin requests and reduces bandwidth costs'.",
  "Cloudflare Learning, 'What is caching?' (https://www.cloudflare.com/learning/cdn/what-is-caching/, fetched 2026-11-24): a CDN 'caches content (such as images, videos, or webpages) in proxy servers that are located closer to end users'; TTL is 'an indication of how long content should be cached', sent in the HTTP header; customers can manually purge content.",
  "Illustration only: Mumbai and New York are an example; 'users may still see the old file until it expires or is purged' follows from TTL caching."
 ],
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Your server is in Mumbai, and a user in New York opens your site. Why is it slower for them? Guess.",
   "caps": "SERVER IN *MUMBAI | USER IN *NEW YORK | WHY *SLOWER?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Distance. Every round trip has to cross the ocean and come back.",
   "caps": "*DISTANCE | EVERY *ROUND TRIP | ACROSS THE *OCEAN"
  },
  {
   "text": "A CDN is a group of servers around the world that keep copies of your content near users.",
   "caps": "A *CDN | SERVERS *WORLDWIDE | COPIES *NEAR USERS"
  },
  {
   "text": "So the New York user gets your images and pages from a server close by.",
   "caps": "SERVED *NEARBY | *IMAGES AND PAGES"
  },
  {
   "text": "And your origin in Mumbai gets far fewer requests, which cuts bandwidth costs too.",
   "caps": "FEWER *ORIGIN REQUESTS | LOWER *BANDWIDTH"
  },
  {
   "text": "But here's the catch: copies can go stale. Each one lives for its TTL, set in the HTTP header.",
   "caps": "THE *CATCH | COPIES GO *STALE | THE *TTL"
  },
  {
   "text": "Change the file before it expires, and some users still see the old one, unless you purge it.",
   "caps": "OLD *VERSION | UNTIL *EXPIRY | OR *PURGE"
  },
  {
   "text": "So cache what rarely changes, and set the TTL on purpose. Did you guess distance?",
   "caps": "CACHE *STATIC FILES | SET THE *TTL | DID YOU GUESS *DISTANCE?"
  }
 ],
